AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000191> "This finding is assessed by gently retracting the oral mucosa from the alveolar ridge. Typically there is a single maxillary and a single mandibular frenulum located in the midline between the two central incisors. Abnormalities of the alveolar ridges may accompany accessory frenula, but these should be assessed separately.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000191> "Accessory oral frenulum")
