AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000396> "This is most often seen in the superior helix where it must be distinguished from a Lop ear (where the usual convexity of the posterior border of the ear is lost). Helix folding is highly variable.")
