AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000506> "Dystopia canthorum (also called telecanthus) describes a subtle but unusual facial feature in which the inner corners of the eyes (canthi) are spaced farther apart than normal, yet the eyes (pupils) themselves are not necessarily widely spaced.")
