# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000703> (Dentinogenesis imperfecta)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9338-3017>) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000703> "Developmental dysplasia of dentin.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000703> "HP:0000703")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000703> "This term is kept for convenience since it is often used to refer to the phenotype of discolored, fragile teeth in the medical literature. Dentinogenesis imperfecta is a disorder of tooth development. This condition causes the teeth to be discolored (most often a blue-gray or yellow-brown color) and translucent. Teeth are also weaker than normal, making them prone to rapid wear, breakage, and loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000703> "Dentinogenesis imperfecta")
