AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0006511> "The laryngeal stridor sound is usually heard during inspiratory phase, also called inspiratory stridor, and may accompanied by inspiratory difficulty in breathing. It may be due to abnormal flaccidity of the epiglottis or arytenoids.")
