AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0009611> "Note that with bifid distal phalanx, the terminal phalanx of the thumb is clefted but is still one bone. With duplication of the terminal phalanx of the thumb, the distal phalanx is split into two bones that are located side by side. With triphalangeal thumb, the thumb has three phalanxes located one after the other.")
